[{:db/id "q-75503/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "5188b779-752e-59af-adb7-07e88b20e763" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75503/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "fbd179bf-3f0c-5ccd-bc4d-4e7719b6f74a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75503/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "836c90b7-51cd-5592-9519-01f54ae64162" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75503/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "389d481b-4ca4-5de0-a180-cc213a1ea9fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75503/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "be38fea0-7670-55d4-be38-274ce30e0aaa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75503/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d9fe597-107a-5f49-b661-72b66ad155a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75503/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer-field/choices ["q-75503/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" "q-75503/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" "q-75503/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" "q-75503/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" "q-75503/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75503" :question/id #uuid "709b5298-f419-5383-8936-25139c2a4a09" :question/math-academy-id "q-75503" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75503/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75503"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-43000"] :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-75496/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "d302cad3-81ec-554b-b797-91cce10d6872" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75496/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "64bb514d-0b9c-5f55-ba8d-8d2903e57f36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75496/selection/a5c92681e90a059a1f14ff8cb6c5effaecb929ee088b17e5d8e66a13154bddef" :answer/id #uuid "ced2c4c3-f009-5aeb-af3b-e7c1e0bd4ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75496/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "cb84f85f-2ab3-5d03-b96d-35da5df9dea5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75496/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "8644fc6d-a846-5da5-b463-aec67c8941d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75496/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a681057a-d2f6-5de8-b5c7-c51163b89190" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75496/selection/a5c92681e90a059a1f14ff8cb6c5effaecb929ee088b17e5d8e66a13154bddef" :answer-field/choices ["q-75496/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-75496/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" "q-75496/selection/a5c92681e90a059a1f14ff8cb6c5effaecb929ee088b17e5d8e66a13154bddef" "q-75496/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" "q-75496/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75496" :question/id #uuid "c1c2183f-2c3e-5666-b1a3-ed31682996f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75496" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 13\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75496/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75496"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131380/selection/ec59a455a2297ed22e1f2c49c621394f33c23c3ed9f526f33537874a54b0aff6" :answer/id #uuid "e213c815-52cb-58e1-bfd8-d4b3b0067b58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131380/selection/c319a4d4309614cb7987ad829693f43c86843cf379b66140205c9d0fc3a4facc" :answer/id #uuid "23af7e0e-3b7a-5ab1-83c7-0ded63a2a811" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131380/selection/9807a9557099656a8d55bffcf17cf5a937595b85b0bcd8db60ad8fde2e9bd5f0" :answer/id #uuid "0aa31754-e114-5f9f-a0f7-26638c423de3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131380/selection/7d609f407ca916ed9d1c5d7866ca31ff76f613b8ec2224ff56fb63ed83808194" :answer/id #uuid "d92c6ef3-dc52-59e4-8daf-26b8990eb382" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131380/selection/9362f748c2a8abbffc4c18a01336d7bc8fc654e842ce01f52b1add87315c617a" :answer/id #uuid "d856643a-37b8-5ad5-863e-75fd769576bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131380/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1bedaad-9c36-5e3f-bfc9-8bb03bf0ddab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131380/selection/c319a4d4309614cb7987ad829693f43c86843cf379b66140205c9d0fc3a4facc" :answer-field/choices ["q-131380/selection/ec59a455a2297ed22e1f2c49c621394f33c23c3ed9f526f33537874a54b0aff6" "q-131380/selection/c319a4d4309614cb7987ad829693f43c86843cf379b66140205c9d0fc3a4facc" "q-131380/selection/9807a9557099656a8d55bffcf17cf5a937595b85b0bcd8db60ad8fde2e9bd5f0" "q-131380/selection/7d609f407ca916ed9d1c5d7866ca31ff76f613b8ec2224ff56fb63ed83808194" "q-131380/selection/9362f748c2a8abbffc4c18a01336d7bc8fc654e842ce01f52b1add87315c617a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131380" :question/id #uuid "69c3d843-e9dd-52a0-9c3a-7112e0ce14b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-131380" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131380/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131380"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131384/selection/44c87af5c3ea161ec8468fcd2aa1cecc3c23bc912177e3acf31b74fa40344cae" :answer/id #uuid "402333e9-bffc-5f6a-b40f-70a6f7f92759" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{E}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131384/selection/12c0339fb0988ec15e3de03eefb6bdaa419ae5e60c2d32bba00069fc210dc72d" :answer/id #uuid "d6529732-9b49-5f7a-ae84-2ee74ff49a59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{E}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131384/selection/f4ece79954c74052d56a15272bd95a736a9f0e91969884a6594809eb27763bcb" :answer/id #uuid "a7cc9629-0092-53a7-bbab-0a2c79ac7d62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{E}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131384/selection/3bee19f064f901d6e5bfe480e4158668e18632bd9b5fa52620b9f07078aa3192" :answer/id #uuid "723f1cdd-d867-5391-96a4-6cfe5c90348d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{E}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131384/selection/8907c27813fe868ae00c9dfa62d5f78c5b9014f43dbcaf5c9413cad4af19c59a" :answer/id #uuid "4b816960-cd52-53da-a63b-345c4979c8b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{E}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131384/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "717058eb-3183-5cd1-bdd6-6107f160ff09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131384/selection/12c0339fb0988ec15e3de03eefb6bdaa419ae5e60c2d32bba00069fc210dc72d" :answer-field/choices ["q-131384/selection/44c87af5c3ea161ec8468fcd2aa1cecc3c23bc912177e3acf31b74fa40344cae" "q-131384/selection/12c0339fb0988ec15e3de03eefb6bdaa419ae5e60c2d32bba00069fc210dc72d" "q-131384/selection/f4ece79954c74052d56a15272bd95a736a9f0e91969884a6594809eb27763bcb" "q-131384/selection/3bee19f064f901d6e5bfe480e4158668e18632bd9b5fa52620b9f07078aa3192" "q-131384/selection/8907c27813fe868ae00c9dfa62d5f78c5b9014f43dbcaf5c9413cad4af19c59a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131384" :question/id #uuid "784f0439-5a9c-50b5-bcf3-3949291e16a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-131384" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $E$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${E}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $E$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $E$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${E}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{E}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131384/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131384"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43005/selection/26314eed91937e6eaf712da2495688ab047adf36b45def4b4f8810982bca25db" :answer/id #uuid "0be9af6a-3f9a-5c67-b6ff-3627dba68379" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43005/selection/4cce7b7bd712e89a5e02d2017a8fd2fb45c0c89acd1bd14671073d997f4e2506" :answer/id #uuid "0791b589-95a8-5d4a-b5a4-9922672dc9bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43005/selection/7c27a0f50e45f4a4183e6c271bc79a19a09c47730cfb4a82834a0bf6799afaba" :answer/id #uuid "3d06e262-0bf4-5196-ac14-a98b3bdb608e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43005/selection/c5875ea7c002f701d36fbcf3fee3978b68b6c154994b8fdd9cc09d30c4f3e88c" :answer/id #uuid "17d4bafd-e317-52cd-a72c-8b0630a380b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43005/selection/648d63d4eb3b9059308e898ca82a582d459d4d1fe84941d35fc60acec49932b8" :answer/id #uuid "35e6c3b0-cd4f-5a87-98e6-bb73f72ab5dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43005/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5120172-51b3-5e24-99fa-5de7583e860b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-43005/selection/c5875ea7c002f701d36fbcf3fee3978b68b6c154994b8fdd9cc09d30c4f3e88c" :answer-field/choices ["q-43005/selection/26314eed91937e6eaf712da2495688ab047adf36b45def4b4f8810982bca25db" "q-43005/selection/4cce7b7bd712e89a5e02d2017a8fd2fb45c0c89acd1bd14671073d997f4e2506" "q-43005/selection/7c27a0f50e45f4a4183e6c271bc79a19a09c47730cfb4a82834a0bf6799afaba" "q-43005/selection/c5875ea7c002f701d36fbcf3fee3978b68b6c154994b8fdd9cc09d30c4f3e88c" "q-43005/selection/648d63d4eb3b9059308e898ca82a582d459d4d1fe84941d35fc60acec49932b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43005" :question/id #uuid "f414baf2-ff37-5d6f-8c93-b84870e3eb0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-43005" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $Q$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${Q}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Q\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,4 & \\,1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,-1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $Q$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $Q$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Q\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,4 & \\,1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,-1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${Q}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{Q}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-43005/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43005"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-43006"] :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $A$ is found using the row operations as shown below. What are the corresponding row operations?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-31945/selection/4afe1492125f638f67b645998946aec3135dbd4b97cd2f89feb7363d8fbd97ab" :answer/id #uuid "50e88431-682f-57ff-8120-e35bc2a9a66b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{3}{4}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31945/selection/68aa1ad1169b72612f62ce110c0f885220f59dd1474b509cf7a1beedbc0c1e22" :answer/id #uuid "4c847502-8514-5d10-9dcd-ee929fb97fb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31945/selection/c871e7b8b7ba0a6e73c9ae735880e6d583fcc7aafd5e0a8341058cc57344b455" :answer/id #uuid "7fb8073e-8de1-5ef6-9e33-e8ba6f5563c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31945/selection/e7e24f3fb65aee5b6e5d7d5b8f1dfd626e065bfcd8391906016bb63b426feb98" :answer/id #uuid "d79f0963-0d1a-5d70-9ac1-20722c6f883b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31945/selection/1f3633bbf528a602a3ab0ad01d88062fb3ccc7e04e6407729490cc8507812ccf" :answer/id #uuid "daa4cb16-32bc-5407-9cba-6ec88a3e6469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31945/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "93d5f24f-9961-5171-9187-5181cc9626d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31945/selection/e7e24f3fb65aee5b6e5d7d5b8f1dfd626e065bfcd8391906016bb63b426feb98" :answer-field/choices ["q-31945/selection/4afe1492125f638f67b645998946aec3135dbd4b97cd2f89feb7363d8fbd97ab" "q-31945/selection/68aa1ad1169b72612f62ce110c0f885220f59dd1474b509cf7a1beedbc0c1e22" "q-31945/selection/c871e7b8b7ba0a6e73c9ae735880e6d583fcc7aafd5e0a8341058cc57344b455" "q-31945/selection/e7e24f3fb65aee5b6e5d7d5b8f1dfd626e065bfcd8391906016bb63b426feb98" "q-31945/selection/1f3633bbf528a602a3ab0ad01d88062fb3ccc7e04e6407729490cc8507812ccf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31945" :question/id #uuid "d8e64088-2308-5369-8285-5d893b0dfcdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-31945" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $K$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to the blank spaces?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $K$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $K$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${K}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{K}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-31945/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31945"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31872/selection/d6b536ea29fc358444202dbfd499be70b04d4eae076b58a35cf0acba4b9fde09" :answer/id #uuid "e62a602d-46e8-5f7d-92b4-d9d9daac470e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31872/selection/a5f407ee259b2fb45867fd574e61447e76e1df1fd7cb13ffb2c1005d56bb5548" :answer/id #uuid "063ab8b7-d4dd-5e4a-893d-3e9a78283611" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31872/selection/cb21307862fd462a77582c8d8644b0acc9761ba8b069e03e3c2bb076ab806c8c" :answer/id #uuid "cacd7b05-3c6b-5e6d-ab18-1916bc907620" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31872/selection/48f8bbdbfee4cecd111e1bd436aa33674564981b056ce1ad7df479a74566607d" :answer/id #uuid "2f2bec2b-1295-561b-88bd-c350975daa7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31872/selection/86d7d2e113393944dbcf41304a4497b73afa81d35165e2d2d2d8a3c9434bdebf" :answer/id #uuid "e5c2a2a3-f14a-5e45-a22b-9a63e207be57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31872/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c20189b7-04e0-57b7-9592-81dfb42ed8e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31872/selection/86d7d2e113393944dbcf41304a4497b73afa81d35165e2d2d2d8a3c9434bdebf" :answer-field/choices ["q-31872/selection/d6b536ea29fc358444202dbfd499be70b04d4eae076b58a35cf0acba4b9fde09" "q-31872/selection/a5f407ee259b2fb45867fd574e61447e76e1df1fd7cb13ffb2c1005d56bb5548" "q-31872/selection/cb21307862fd462a77582c8d8644b0acc9761ba8b069e03e3c2bb076ab806c8c" "q-31872/selection/48f8bbdbfee4cecd111e1bd436aa33674564981b056ce1ad7df479a74566607d" "q-31872/selection/86d7d2e113393944dbcf41304a4497b73afa81d35165e2d2d2d8a3c9434bdebf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31872" :question/id #uuid "0ac0783b-5b73-5c8c-959b-6029e5d56c68" :question/math-academy-id "q-31872" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $J$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to the blank spaces?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[J\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $J$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $J$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[J\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${J}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{J}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{6} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-31872/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4725"] :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2 \\,$ and $\\, R_2 :=  R_2+(-1)R_1?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080619/assets/e607bba88cc1f15abaa45fc3cf02110243433d60259c56805515ced373054ca0.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4724"] :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080619/assets/89189584fab0cbb79fb0b4ac30a81b41bfd6508de7499c111fd53fb6c0c2c928.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4723"] :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{2}R_1,\n\\qquad\nR_1 := R_1+(-3)R_2.\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080619/assets/0a034d98da82572a523d406379ab286d1af6b37820f5c2380822abf611643f83.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
